### 3.1 Authentication & User Profiles (P0) — Partly built
- **Built:** sign up and sign in with email and password; email confirmation required before writing reviews or
  enquiries. Roles: parent, school_admin (a school's staff), admin (Kidscover); users cannot change their own role.
- **Built:** settings — the language of the whole app, notifications on or off, unlocking with a fingerprint or face,
  and deleting the account and everything in it.
- **Not started:** Google, Microsoft and phone (OTP) sign-in; a profile picture or stock avatar; dark mode.

### 3.2 Location-Based Discovery (P0) — Built
- **Use my location:** the phone's position (rounded to about 100 m) is used only to measure distance; it is never
  stored in the database or on the phone. Refusing permission leaves everything else working.
- **Distance on every school, "Nearest first", "Within 2 / 5 / 10 km"** (straight-line, labelled as such). Schools
  without coordinates are left out of near-me lists only.
- **Drive time by car** (Google Routes API, traffic-aware), in three framings: "Weekday 7:30 am" (the next school-run
  departure, India time), "Right now", and **"By the time school starts"** — which reads each school's own start time
  and answers "leave by 7:12 to reach 8:00", grouping schools that start at the same time into one lookup. When a
  school has not given its start time, 8:00 am is assumed and labelled as an assumption.
- **Dashboard tiles** above the list: how many schools are in the area on screen, how many have admissions open, and
  how many have given their fees — counted in the database.
- **Cost control:** limits in the database, changeable by an admin: 20 lookups per parent per day and 500 schools per
  day for the whole app by default. Kidscover stores only a count of lookups per parent per day, never where anyone was.
- **Not started:** a location fallback order (GPS > address book > last session > ask). Today it is GPS, or search by
  name and area.

### 3.3 Discover List, Categories & Filters (P0) — Built
- **Categories:** every place is a *school* (preschool to class 12, junior colleges included), an *after-school class*
  (music, dance, sports, art, abacus, tuition) or a *college* (degree, engineering, business, law, medicine, teacher
  training). The app opens on Schools; the other two are one tap away. Places not for children (driving schools, gyms,
  IELTS classes, shops, offices) are hidden.
- **Search** by name or area; **filters:** level (preschool, primary, secondary, not stated), daycare, board (with
  "also show schools whose board is not known yet"), Google rating (with "include unrated"), **first-year cost** (with
  "also show schools whose fees nobody has given yet"), admissions open, sort (A to Z, best rated, nearest, lowest
  cost). Level, daycare, board and cost apply to schools only and are set aside, not cleared, on the other lists.
- **Not started:** filtering by how long the institution has been established.

### 3.4 School Detail Page (P1) — Built
- **Photo:** uploaded by the school (it confirms it may publish it) or a free-licensed Wikimedia Commons photo shown
  with its author and licence; with no photo, a drawn school in colours of its own. No paid or copyrighted image
  sources.
- **Facts, each with its source:** levels (set by the school or Kidscover if they have set them; otherwise from the
  name, Google and, once accepted, the school's website); board ("confirmed by CBSE's own record", "from the school's
  website", "from the school's name"); admission status with year ("from the school's website, checked Sep 2026");
  Google rating; parent reviews; the time the school day starts.
- **Facilities** (20 kinds: cafeteria, open and indoor play, pool, courts, library, science / computer / maths / STEM /
  AI labs, smart classrooms, auditorium, art and music rooms, school bus, medical room, CCTV, air conditioning,
  special needs support, teacher-student ratio).
- **Achievements** the school claims: class 10 and class 12 results, college placements, notable alumni, awards;
  newest first; each marked with its source and linked to where it was published.
- **The cost of a year**, broken down (see 3.11), and **comparing up to four schools side by side** — cost, distance,
  drive time, levels, board, admissions, both ratings and the start of the school day, in one scrolling table.
- **Ask about admissions** and **apply with the Kidscover Standard form** (schools only), and the school's website link.
- **Not started:** enrolment size (how many children the school has).

### 3.5 Admissions Enquiries (P1) — Built
- A short form (which class, roughly when, the question). It deliberately does **not** ask for a child's name or date
  of birth.
- A conversation per school under **Enquiries**, with an unread count. Replies show as coming from "the school". One
  open enquiry per school; at most 10 new enquiries a day; a confirmed email is required; either side can close,
  writing again reopens.
- **Answered by the school itself** where the school has staff on Kidscover, and by Kidscover staff where it does not.
  A school's staff never see the parent's email address; Kidscover admins do.
- **Partner Portal inbox** for answering, with "need a reply" counts, and a nudge that sends the parent's phone a
  notification.

### 3.6 Parent Reviews & Moderation (P1) — Built
- Anonymous reviews (rating, optional title, text, relationship to the school), one per parent per school; a new or
  edited review is pending until a moderator publishes it; parents can report others' reviews; the Parent Reviews tab
  in the portal publishes, rejects and handles reports.

### 3.7 School Data Pipeline — Built
- **Import:** Google Places (Mumbai / Thane box) for names, addresses, coordinates, types and ratings.
- **Quality rules and categories** in the database (from the name first, Google's type second); an admin can move any
  single place or hide it, with a reason shown for every automatic decision.
- **Website reader** (edge function, run by an admin in batches): obeys robots.txt, identifies itself, reads the home
  page and up to three more pages per school, refuses private addresses (by name **and** by the address they resolve
  to) and re-checks redirects. It finds:
  - **Board:** English, Marathi and Hindi wording, and CBSE affiliation numbers checked against CBSE's public record
    (confirmed only when the record is in Maharashtra and matches the PIN, website or name).
  - **Levels:** ranges such as "Nursery to Grade 10", "Classes I to X" and "iyatta 5 vi te 10 vi", plus named sections.
  - **Admission status** with its year; old notices are marked and cannot be used.
  - **Facilities**, including a teacher-student ratio.
  - **Claimed achievements.**

  On a website shared by several schools, only this school's pages are read.
- **Review:** everything found waits in the School Data tab with the sentence and page it came from; nothing reaches
  parents until an admin accepts it; what the school or Kidscover entered is never overwritten by a website finding.
  Schools are re-read every 30 days.
- **Not used (and not worked around):** the CISCE directory (behind a CAPTCHA), open UDISE+ extracts (no board column,
  no licence), and parts of CBSE's site that refuse automated access.

### 3.8 School Profiles, School Staff & the Change Log — Built
- A Kidscover admin adds a school's staff by email (they sign up first); staff can edit only their own school: levels,
  photo, facilities, achievements, fees and the start of the school day.
- Levels set by hand (daycare, preschool, primary, secondary) replace the automatic ones, so a school whose name and
  website say nothing can still be found under the right level, and a wrong level can be removed. "Back to automatic"
  returns the school to the rules.
- Changes go live at once. Database triggers record every change (who, their role, when, before and after), so nothing
  escapes the log. A Kidscover admin sees all changes, and can undo the latest change to anything; the undo is logged
  too.
- Photos upload to a public storage bucket, one folder per school, JPEG / PNG / WebP up to 5 MB; only that school's
  staff (or an admin) can write to its folder, and only an address on Kidscover's own storage is accepted.

### 3.9 Look and Feel — Built
- A warm palette (violet, coral, sunshine and mint on lavender), a logo, a welcome drawing of a parent walking a child
  to school on the sign-in screen, a welcome banner that changes with the list, a picture on every school card, and
  icons for categories, facilities and achievements. All drawings are made in code, so there is nothing to license.

### 3.10 Partner Portal (Admin Web App) — Built
- **Kidscover admin tabs:** Admissions Pipeline; Admissions Enquiries (inbox); Applications; Parent Reviews
  (moderation); School Data (website reader and review); Categories; School Profiles (edit any school, staff, fees,
  the school day, the school's own system, outbound clicks, change log with undo); Security.
- **Panels:** data pipeline sweep, and drive-time usage and limits with a live test button.
- **School staff** get their own dashboard showing only their school: its enquiries, its applications, its profile and
  its fees.

### 3.11 Fees and the True Cost of a Year — Built
- Each school gives its fees per level (daycare, preschool, primary, secondary) in the Partner Portal: tuition, school
  bus, meals, uniform and books, activities, other yearly fees, and the one-time admission and registration fees. A
  refundable deposit is shown but never counted as a cost.
- Parents see **the first year** (everything, including the one-time fees) and **each year after that**, with the
  breakdown underneath and where the numbers came from.
- They can filter by what they can spend, sort by lowest cost, and choose whether to include schools whose fees
  nobody has given yet.

### 3.12 The Kidscover Standard Admission Form — Built
- One form per child and school: the child's name, date of birth, class and year, the parent's name, phone, email and
  address, and anything they want the school to know. The parent ticks a box naming the school before it is sent.
- Only that parent, that school's staff and a Kidscover admin can ever read it. The family can withdraw it or delete
  it outright at any time.
- The school moves it through its stages (being looked at, visit arranged, a place offered, waiting list, accepted,
  not offered) with a line back to the family; every stage is kept for the family to see.
- **The school's own system:** a Kidscover admin can connect an https address; each application is sent there as JSON,
  signed with that school's own secret (HMAC-SHA256), retried with a growing wait, never following a redirect and
  never to an address inside a private network. The secret is shown once.
- **Going out to a school's own pages** is counted (website, admissions page, fee page), so a school can see the
  interest Kidscover sends it. Counts only: never who clicked.

### 3.13 Notifications — Built
- A parent's phone is told when a school replies to their enquiry, or moves their application along.
- Notifications never carry the words of a message: "the school replied", never what was said.
- Each one is sent in the parent's own language, from the same translations the app itself uses, so the notification
  and the screen it opens always say the same thing. They can switch them off in Settings.

### 3.14 Languages — Built
- 31: English, the 22 languages of the Eighth Schedule of the Constitution, and Arabic, Chinese, French, German,
  Japanese, Portuguese, Russian and Spanish. **All 31 are translated**; nothing falls back to English any more.
- Chosen on the sign-in screen or in Settings, saved with the profile, so it follows the parent to a new phone.
- Arabic, Urdu, Kashmiri and Sindhi lay the screen out right to left. Money and dates follow the language.
- Text people type (reviews, achievements, addresses) is shown as written; nothing is machine-translated.
- **Before a public launch, a native speaker should read each language.** They were translated carefully, but a school
  application is not the place for a clumsy sentence.

### 3.15 Security — Built
- Two-step sign-in for the Partner Portal, and a switch that requires it for every Kidscover admin and school staff
  member.
- Every right nobody needs was taken away from the database roles, including the ones Supabase grants by default.
- A parent can delete their account and everything in it, after entering their password again.
- On the phone, the sign-in is encrypted with a key in the phone's own keystore, and can be locked behind a
  fingerprint.
- The full review, what it found and what only the project owner can do: **SECURITY.md**.

