## 6. Technical Architecture

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Parent app | React Native (Expo SDK 57), a single `App.js`; react-native-svg for the drawings; expo-secure-store and expo-local-authentication for the locked sign-in; expo-notifications for push |
| Partner Portal | Next.js (React), with security headers and a content security policy |
| Backend / database | Supabase: PostgreSQL with row level security, SQL functions and triggers, Storage (school photos), Auth (including two-step sign-in) |
| Server functions | Supabase Edge Functions (Deno): commute-times (Google Routes), read-school-websites (the reader), ingest-mumbai-schools, send-push (Expo push), crm-deliver (a school's own system), delete-account |
| App delivery | EAS Build for the Android APK; EAS Update for over-the-air changes to the app's own code |
| Integrations | Google Places API, Google Routes API (computeRouteMatrix), CBSE SARAS record, Wikimedia Commons API, Expo push service, Firebase Cloud Messaging (Android delivery) |

**Database changes** ship as numbered migrations (`supabase/migrations/`), run in order in the Supabase SQL Editor;
each is safe to run more than once.

