## 8. What is live, and what is merged but waiting on a setup step

Everything in §3 marked *Built* is merged to main and tested. Some of it needs a one-time action before a parent can
see it, because migrations and edge functions are deployed by hand.

| Part | State |
|---|---|
| The MVP: discovery, categories, filters, school pages, enquiries, reviews, the website reader, school profiles, staff, the change log, levels by hand | **Live** — migrations to 20260919001400 run, functions deployed, in use |
| Fees, applications, notifications, languages, security, tiles, arrive-by, comparing schools | **Merged.** Needs migrations `20260920000100`–`20260920000600` run in order; `send-push`, `crm-deliver` and `delete-account` deployed; `commute-times` and `read-school-websites` redeployed; the secret `SB_SECRET_KEY` set |
| A notification actually arriving on a phone | Also needs a Firebase project connected to the EAS build, and ideally `EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN` |
| Two-step sign-in required for everyone who works on families' details | Merged; switch it on in the portal's **Security** tab |
| The profile and the address book (a parent's name, how they are addressed, their picture, and the places they search from) | **Merged.** Needs migrations `20260921000100` and `20260921000200` run |
| Photographs of parents and children | **Merged.** Needs migration `20260921000300` run, and `delete-account` deployed so closing an account takes the files with it |
| The app on a real phone | Needs an APK from `eas build --platform android --profile preview` |

**None of these is a code change.** Until they are done, the second-phase features exist in main and in the tests, but
not in front of a parent.

